// Paper II+III: Antifragility as sovereign immune system and stress response.
// "That which does not kill the organism makes it stronger" — Taleb, NOVA edition.
//
// The AntifragilityEngine is the immune system of the FusionOrganism.
// Every output generated by any paper engine passes through this module
// before being returned to a caller. Outputs that survive stress tests
// are φ-boosted; outputs that break are quarantined and logged.
//
// Architecture:
//   STRESS_TEST    — inject controlled perturbation, measure response
//   FRAGILITY_SCORE— score any computation result on fragility spectrum
//   RESILIENCE_BOOST — apply φ-weighted resilience multiplier on survivors
//   IMMUNE_MEMORY  — rolling 64-entry log of stressors + outcomes
//   ANTIFRAGILE_GAIN — measure how much the system GAINED from stress
//
// φ-axis: fragility → robustness → antifragility
//   score < 0     → FRAGILE   (hurts from randomness)
//   score = 0     → ROBUST    (no effect from randomness)
//   score > 0     → ANTIFRAGILE (gains from randomness)
//
